@startuml
title Corda to Solana Bridge Sequence Diagram

box "Corda (+bridge) Users" #pink
actor "Alice\n<Corda Account>\n<Solana Account>" as Alice
actor "Charlie\n<Corda Account>" as Charlie
end box

box "Solana User" #pink
actor "Bob (Solana trader)\n<Solana Account>" as Bob
end box

box "Trusted Corda Nodes" #LightGreen
participant "Legacy Corda Notary" as LN
participant "Bridging Authority\n<Corda participant>" as BA
participant "Solana Trusted Notary\n<Corda Node>\n<Solana Account>" as SN
end box


box "Solana Infrastructure" #lightblue
participant "RPC Provider\n(e.g., Helius, Infura)" as RPC
participant "Solana Network" as SOL
end box


' == Phase 0: Transfer assets ==
' Charlie -> Alice: Propose Corda asset transfer\n(e.g., cash, bond)
' Alice -> Charlie: Sign transaction
' Charlie -> LN: Send transaction for notarization
' LN -> LN: Verify uniqueness,\nadd new TXID to DB
' LN -> Charlie: Notarize and confirm transaction
' Charlie -> Alice: Notify transfer complete

== Phase 0: Prepare for Bridging ==

Alice -> BA: Communicate own Solana PubKey for ATA

== Phase 1: Bridging Corda Asset to Solana ==
autonumber "<b>(B##)"

Alice -> BA: <color brown>**DFC2S_TRANSFER_STATE**</color>\nTransfer Corda state to\nbridging authority (Tx A)
note right of BA
	<color red>**🔒 LOCK PHASE:**</color>
	Original Corda tokens are held by
	Bridge Authority's Locking Identity
	(remain locked while liquid on Solana)
	
	Triggered by: [[https://github.com/corda/corda-solana-toolkit/blob/main/bridging-token-workflows/src/main/kotlin/com/r3/corda/lib/solana/bridging/token/flows/BridgingService.kt#L286 BridgingService.callBridgeFlow()]]
end note

opt Optional: Notary change
BA->Alice: Gather signature for notary change
Alice -> BA: Send signature
BA -> Charlie: Gather signature for notary change
note right of Charlie: <b>Threat:</b> Non-collaboration from Charlie\n(Charlie may refuse to send signature,\npreventing notary change and bridging)
Charlie -> BA: Send signature


BA -> LN: Request notarisation of notary-change tx\n(move state to Solana notary)
LN -> BA: Return notary signature (finalised tx)
BA -> SN: Record/inform new notary\n(notary-change tx)
end

BA -> BA: Lookup/create confidential\nidentity for sender
note right of BA
	[[https://github.com/corda/corda-solana-toolkit/blob/main/bridging-token-workflows/src/main/kotlin/com/r3/corda/lib/solana/bridging/token/flows/BridgeFungibleTokenFlow.kt#L52 BridgeFungibleTokenFlow.call()]]
	[[https://github.com/corda/corda-solana-toolkit/blob/main/bridging-token-workflows/src/main/kotlin/com/r3/corda/lib/solana/bridging/token/flows/ConfigHandler.kt#L77 ConfigHandler.getLockingIdentity()]]
end note
BA -> BA: <color purple>**Create BridgedFungibleTokenProxy**</color>\n(mirrors Corda token + Solana mint metadata)
note right of BA
	<color purple>**Proxy State Created:**</color>
	[[https://github.com/corda/corda-solana-toolkit/blob/main/bridging-token-contracts/src/main/kotlin/com/r3/corda/lib/solana/bridging/token/states/BridgedFungibleTokenProxy.kt BridgedFungibleTokenProxy]]
	• amount: token quantity
	• bridgeTokenAccount: destination on Solana
	• mintAccount: Solana mint pubkey
	• mintAuthority: bridge's mint authority
	
	Flow: [[https://github.com/corda/corda-solana-toolkit/blob/main/bridging-token-workflows/src/main/kotlin/com/r3/corda/lib/solana/bridging/token/flows/MoveAndLockFungibleTokenFlow.kt MoveAndLockFungibleTokenFlow]]
	Contracts:
	[[https://github.com/corda/corda-solana-toolkit/blob/main/bridging-token-contracts/src/main/kotlin/com/r3/corda/lib/solana/bridging/token/contracts/FungibleTokenBridgeContract.kt FungibleTokenBridgeContract.LockToken]]
	[[https://github.com/corda/corda-solana-toolkit/blob/main/bridging-token-contracts/src/main/kotlin/com/r3/corda/lib/solana/bridging/token/contracts/FungibleTokenRedemptionContract.kt FungibleTokenRedemptionContract]]
end note
BA -> SN: <color brown>**DFC2S_NOTARISE_REQUEST**</color>\nSend <color purple>**proxy state**</color> transaction for\nnotarisation and bridging
note right of BA
	[[https://github.com/corda/corda-solana-toolkit/blob/main/bridging-token-workflows/src/main/kotlin/com/r3/corda/lib/solana/bridging/token/flows/BridgeFungibleTokenFlow.kt#L93 BridgeFungibleTokenFlow.createMintTransaction()]]
end note
SN -> SN: Build Solana transaction\n(commit + mint_to)
note right of SN
	<color purple>**Proxy Consumed:**</color>
	BridgedFungibleTokenProxy consumed
	(no outputs - tokens minted on Solana)
	
	Contract Validation:
	[[https://github.com/corda/corda-solana-toolkit/blob/main/bridging-token-contracts/src/main/kotlin/com/r3/corda/lib/solana/bridging/token/contracts/FungibleTokenBridgeContract.kt#L35 FungibleTokenBridgeContract.verifyMintToSolana()]]
end note
SN -> SN: Sign with notary key (commit)\n and mint authority (mint_to)
SN -> RPC: <color brown>**DFC2S_SEND_SOLANA_TX**</color>\nSubmit Solana transaction
RPC -> SOL: Forward transaction
SOL -> RPC: Transaction result
RPC -> SN: <color brown>**DFC2S_CONF_SOLANA_TX**</color>\nConfirm transaction
note right of RPC
	<color orange>**⚠️ TRUST ASSUMPTION:**</color>
	RPC Provider is trusted to:
	• Accurately relay blockchain state
	• Not suppress/fabricate events
	• Maintain availability
end note
SN -> BA: <color brown>**DFC2S_NOTIF_BRIDGE_OK**</color>\nNotify bridging complete
BA -> Alice: <color brown>**DFC2S_NOTIF_USER_BRIDGE_OK**</color>\nNotify bridging complete
SOL -> Alice: <color brown>**DFC2S_MINT_TOKEN**</color>\nMinted Solana token credited\nto Alice' (STH)
note over Alice, SOL
	<color green>**✓ 1:1 Peg Maintained:**</color>
	• Original Corda tokens: LOCKED by BA
	• Reference Solana tokens: LIQUID (tradeable)
	• Equal amounts on both chains
end note

== Phase 2: Solana Token Transfer/Swap (Optional) ==
autonumber "<b>(T##)"

Alice -> Bob: <color brown>**DFC2S_TRANSFER_SOLANA_TOKEN**</color>\nTransfer/SWAP Solana token\n(e.g., for stablecoin)
note over Bob: Now Bob' (Bob) is the\nSolana token holder
note right of Bob #LightCoral
	**Bridge Design Constraint:**
	Bob cannot redeem to his own Corda identity.
	Redemption unlocks tokens to the ORIGINAL
	Corda holder (Alice's locking identity).
	
	Bob must coordinate with Alice off-chain
	to obtain redemption address and agree
	on settlement terms.
end note

== Phase 2A: Redemption Wallet Setup (One-Time Configuration) ==
autonumber "<b>(S##)"

note over BA, Alice #Wheat
	**Pre-requisite for Redemption**
	Redemption wallet addresses must be created
	and mapped to Corda holders before redemption
end note

BA -> BA: Create Solana redemption wallet(s)
note right of BA
	Bridge Authority generates/provisions
	dedicated Solana wallet keypairs:
	• redemptionWalletAccount (Pubkey)
	• One per holder or shared pool
	• Owned by Bridge Authority
	
	**⚠️ MANUAL PROCESS - NOT AUTOMATED**
	Keypairs created externally, not by code
end note

BA -> SOL: Create Associated Token Account (ATA)
note right of BA
	Token2022.createAssociatedTokenAccount(
	  redemptionWalletAccount,
	  mintAccount
	) → redemptionTokenAccount
	
	Implementation:
	[[https://github.com/corda/corda-solana-toolkit/blob/main/bridging-token-workflows/src/main/kotlin/com/r3/corda/lib/solana/bridging/token/flows/TokenAccountService.kt#L47 TokenAccountService.createAta()]]
	
	**⚠️ MANUAL EXECUTION REQUIRED**
end note
SOL -> BA: redemptionTokenAccount created

BA -> BA: Configure holder mappings
note right of BA
	[[https://github.com/corda/corda-solana-toolkit/blob/main/bridging-token-workflows/src/main/kotlin/com/r3/corda/lib/solana/bridging/token/flows/ConfigHandler.kt#L44 ConfigHandler.redemptionWalletAccountToHolder]]
	
	redemptionWalletAccountToHolder = {
	  "AliceRedemptionPubkey": "O=Alice,L=London,C=GB"
	}
	
	Maps Solana addresses → Corda X500 names
	**Manual configuration in CorDapp config**
end note

BA -> BA: Start WebSocket subscription
note right of BA
	[[https://github.com/corda/corda-solana-toolkit/blob/main/bridging-token-workflows/src/main/kotlin/com/r3/corda/lib/solana/bridging/token/flows/BridgingService.kt#L102 BridgingService.onStartup()]]
	[[https://github.com/corda/corda-solana-toolkit/blob/main/bridging-token-workflows/src/main/kotlin/com/r3/corda/lib/solana/bridging/token/flows/BridgingService.kt#L130 socket.onToken2022ByOwner()]]
	
	Subscribe to Token2022 program accounts
	for each redemptionWalletAccount
	
	WebSocket Implementation:
	[[https://github.com/corda/corda-solana-toolkit/blob/main/bridging-token-workflows/src/main/kotlin/com/r3/corda/lib/solana/bridging/token/flows/SavaFactory.kt#L30 SavaFactory.WebSocketWrapper.onToken2022ByOwner()]]
end note

BA -> Alice: Communicate redemption address
note right of Alice
	<color blue>**Out-of-band communication:**</color>
	Bridge Authority provides:
	• redemptionWalletAccount (Pubkey)
	• Redemption process instructions
	
	Alice must send tokens to THIS address
	to initiate redemption
end note

note over BA, Alice #LightGreen
	**Setup Complete**
	Users know where to send tokens
	Bridge Authority monitors addresses
end note

== Phase 3: Redemption (Solana Asset Back to Corda) ==

autonumber "<b>(R##)"

note across
	**Redemption Address Communication** DFC2S_SEND_REDEEM_ADDR
	**OUT-OF-BAND COMMUNICATION REQUIRED**
	Bob needs Alice's redemption address to initiate redemption. This information is NOT available on-chain or deterministic.
	**Threat:** Stale, incorrect, or unavailable redemption address causes DoS or loss of funds.
end note



BA -> RPC: <color brown>**DFC2S_POLL_REDEMPTION**</color>\nWebSocket subscription +\nperiodic RPC polling
note right of RPC
	<color orange>**⚠️ NOT CRYPTOGRAPHICALLY SIGNED:**</color>
	WebSocket events are JSON-RPC responses,
	not blockchain-signed data.
	Must verify state independently.
end note
note right of BA
	Monitoring:
	[[https://github.com/corda/corda-solana-toolkit/blob/main/bridging-token-workflows/src/main/kotlin/com/r3/corda/lib/solana/bridging/token/flows/BridgingService.kt BridgingService]]
end note
RPC -> BA: <color brown>**DFC2S_NOTIF_BALANCE**</color>\nNotify non-zero balance\n(WebSocket event)
note right of BA
	[[https://github.com/corda/corda-solana-toolkit/blob/main/bridging-token-workflows/src/main/kotlin/com/r3/corda/lib/solana/bridging/token/flows/BridgingService.kt#L175 BridgingService.processRedemptionEvent()]]
end note
BA -> BA: Vault query for bridged\nstates (for Alice)
BA -> BA: Create Corda transaction\n(un-bridge state + Solana burn instruction)
note right of BA
	[[https://github.com/corda/corda-solana-toolkit/blob/main/bridging-token-workflows/src/main/kotlin/com/r3/corda/lib/solana/bridging/token/flows/BridgingService.kt#L223 BridgingService.callRedemptionFlow()]]
	Initiates: [[https://github.com/corda/corda-solana-toolkit/blob/main/bridging-token-workflows/src/main/kotlin/com/r3/corda/lib/solana/bridging/token/flows/RedeemFungibleTokenFlow.kt RedeemFungibleTokenFlow]]
end note
BA -> SN: <color brown>**DFC2S_REDEEM_REQUEST**</color>\nSend transaction for\natomic redemption
note right of BA
	[[https://github.com/corda/corda-solana-toolkit/blob/main/bridging-token-workflows/src/main/kotlin/com/r3/corda/lib/solana/bridging/token/flows/RedeemFungibleTokenFlow.kt RedeemFungibleTokenFlow]]
	Creates burn receipt and unlock transaction
end note
SN -> SN: Build Solana transaction\n(commit + burn)
note right of SN
	Contract Validation:
	[[https://github.com/corda/corda-solana-toolkit/blob/main/bridging-token-contracts/src/main/kotlin/com/r3/corda/lib/solana/bridging/token/contracts/FungibleTokenRedemptionContract.kt#L32 FungibleTokenRedemptionContract.verifyBurnOnSolana()]]
	[[https://github.com/corda/corda-solana-toolkit/blob/main/bridging-token-contracts/src/main/kotlin/com/r3/corda/lib/solana/bridging/token/contracts/FungibleTokenRedemptionContract.kt#L25 FungibleTokenRedemptionContract.verifyUnlockToken()]]
end note
SN -> SN: Sign with notary key (commit) \nand redemption owner key (burn)
SN -> RPC: <color brown>**DFC2S_SEND_BURN_TX**</color>\nSubmit Solana transaction
RPC -> SOL: Forward burn transaction
SOL -> RPC: Burn result
RPC -> SN: <color brown>**DFC2S_CONF_BURN_TX**</color>\nConfirm transaction
SN -> BA: <color brown>**DFC2S_NOTIF_REDEMPTION_OK**</color>\nNotify redemption complete
BA -> Bob: <color brown>**DFC2S_NOTIF_USER_RED_OK**</color>\nNotify redemption complete\n(Bob' redeemed)
note over BA, Bob
	<color red>**🔓 UNLOCK PHASE:**</color>
	• Solana tokens: BURNED
	• Original Corda tokens: UNLOCKED
	• Transferred to redemption holder
end note

BA -> Alice: <color brown>**DFC2S_FINALITY_REDEEM**</color>\nFinalityFlow notification\n(tokens received)
note right of Alice
	<color green>**Token SDK FinalityFlow:**</color>
	MoveFungibleTokens includes FinalityFlow
	which notifies the receiver (Alice) and
	stores the new token states in her vault.
	Alice does NOT need to sign.
end note
@enduml